<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices steady on lower arrivals.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices steady on lower arrivals.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices were steady in limited trad and low arrivals on Monday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices fell on increased selling with soyoil solvent down 200 rupees per tonne and soyoil refined down by 300 rupees.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices firmed on good export demand. Soymeal yellow was $293-295 per tonne for the current season and $276-278 for the new November-December season. Rapeseed extraction was $128-130 in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,500 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4,450 rupees FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
